## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
Implement GitHub issue #55: live line-buffered terminal input on Firefox 153+ without changing Chromium behavior or expanding into Firefox file persistence.

### Decisions Made
- Kept SharedArrayBuffer/Atomics as the first transport so Chromium behavior and request shape remain unchanged.
- Added a separate session-scoped postMessage transport because Firefox extension pages cannot rely on SharedArrayBuffer.
- Used worker-side detection of both WebAssembly.Suspending and WebAssembly.promising as the execution authority, with Firefox 153 as the UI support floor.
- Retained buffered stdin for older or JSPI-disabled Firefox environments.
- Added per-run session IDs and EOF rejection so stale or post-completion input cannot cross process boundaries.

### Trade-offs
- Input is canonical and line-buffered, not a raw POSIX PTY.
- Real Firefox JSPI runtime acceptance remains manual because the repository smoke harness validates Firefox packaging rather than executing the extension.

